Assertions:
[STATUS] login response status is 200 with succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a record exists for the user with signInType="Password", succeeded=true and failureReason empty {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the record carries createdDate, ipAddress, host and userAgent {OBSERVED}

[BODY] a record exists with failureReason="UserNotFound" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] userId is null — the account does not exist, so there is nothing to attribute the row to {OBSERVED}
[BODY] userName is preserved exactly as it was typed {OBSERVED}
[BODY] storeId, memberId and organizationId are empty on this row {SPEC}

[BODY] the first failures are recorded with failureReason="InvalidPassword" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] once the account is locked, subsequent attempts are recorded with failureReason="LockedOut" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the transition happens once — there is no attempt recorded with both reasons {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] refresh response status is 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the search returns no rows for that account after T0 — token rotation is deliberately not recorded {SPEC}
[BODY] the scope is the account plus a time window, so a sign-in by another suite running in parallel cannot satisfy or break this assertion {SPEC}

[BODY] the number of records equals the number of attempts performed, exactly {OBSERVED}
[BODY] no two records share the same createdDate and type for a single attempt {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the records appear in the order the attempts were made {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] impersonate response status is 200 and carries an access_token for the customer {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a record exists with signInType="Impersonation" and succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[BODY] userName is the CUSTOMER and operatorUserName is the OPERATOR — the two are not interchangeable {SPEC}
[BODY] operatorUserId is populated {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] response status is 200 and returns a token for the operator {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a record exists with signInType="ImpersonationRevert" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] userName is the customer being LEFT and operatorUserName is the real operator {SPEC}

[STATUS] response status is 200 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] one additional Impersonation record exists for the refresh {SPEC}
[BODY] operatorUserName on that record is still the original operator — rotation does not lose the attribution {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] response status is 401 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a record exists with signInType="Impersonation", succeeded=false and failureReason="Forbidden" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] operatorUserName is empty — there is no operator to name on an unauthenticated probe {SPEC}

[STATUS] response status is 400 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a record exists with failureReason="UserNotFound" and signInType="Impersonation" {OBSERVED}
[BODY] userId falls back to the id that was attempted, so the probe is traceable {SPEC}

[BODY] that session carries isImpersonated=true {OBSERVED}
[BODY] operatorUserName on the session is the operator who opened it {OBSERVED}
[BODY] an ordinary, non-impersonated session of the same user carries isImpersonated=false {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] the terminate call returns 204 {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] the refresh afterwards is refused with 400 — the session is gone {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the session no longer appears in the sessions search for that user {OBSERVED}

[STATUS] the search endpoint answers 403 {OBSERVED}
[STATUS] the stats endpoint answers 403 {OBSERVED}
[BODY] no record data is returned in either response {OBSERVED}

[BODY] Record sign-in attempts is Boolean with default true {SPEC}
[BODY] Keep records for (days) is Integer with default 30 {SPEC}
[BODY] Clean up old sign-in records is Boolean with default true {SPEC}
[BODY] the cleanup cron is a Cron setting with default "0 1 */1 * *" {SPEC}
[BODY] all four report groupName "Platform|Sign In Log" {OBSERVED}

[BODY] records older than the retention window are gone {SPEC}
[BODY] records inside the window survive {SPEC}
[BODY] with retention set to 0 or less, nothing is deleted at all {SPEC}

[DOM] the group is titled "Platform > Sign In Log" {OBSERVED}
[DOM] controls "Cron for the sign-in log cleanup job", "Clean up old sign-in records", "Record sign-in attempts", "Keep records for (days)" are present {SPEC}
[DOM] the cron field shows a human-readable "Runs:" line for the expression it holds {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the changed retention value survives reopening the group {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the "Cron for the sign-in log cleanup job" field holds the new expression after the restart {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the "Runs:" preview describes the new schedule rather than the old one {SPEC}
[STATE] the cleanup job next runs at the new time, not the previous one {SPEC}

[BODY] every row in the succeeded=true result has succeeded=true {OBSERVED}
[BODY] every row in the succeeded=false result has succeeded=false {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the two counts add up to the total for the same closed window — no row falls outside the partition {SPEC}

[BODY] the On behalf filter returns grants only — no revert rows {SPEC}
[BODY] the On behalf revert filter returns reverts only {SPEC}
[BODY] asking for both types returns the sum of the two, so a caller that wants the whole picture still can {OBSERVED}

[BODY] withoutStore=true returns only rows whose storeId is empty {SPEC}
[BODY] withoutStore=false returns only rows that belong to a store {SPEC}
[BODY] the two add up to the total for the same closed window {SPEC}
[BODY] filtering by a named store returns only that store's rows {OBSERVED}

[BODY] the search totalCount equals the count the panel reported {SPEC}
[BODY] every returned row has that exact userName — accounts that merely contain it as a substring are not returned {SPEC}
[BODY] rows where the account is only the OPERATOR of an on-behalf session are not returned {SPEC}

[BODY] searching an operator name returns on-behalf rows whose userName is a different account {SPEC}
[BODY] searching an IP returns the rows from that address {OBSERVED}
[BODY] searching a user name returns that account's rows {OBSERVED}

[BODY] createdDate descends through the first page {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the second page returns a different set of ids — no overlap with the first {OBSERVED}
[BODY] totalCount is the same on both calls {OBSERVED}

[BODY] impersonationCount equals the search totalCount {SPEC}
[BODY] revert records are excluded from both — a revert ends a session rather than opening one {SPEC}
[BODY] denied impersonation attempts are excluded from both — they open nothing {SPEC}

[BODY] totalCount, failedCount, distinctUserCount and impersonationCount are returned {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the matching previous-period counters are returned and use the same counting rule as the current ones {SPEC}
[BODY] topFailedIpAddresses, topFailedUserNames, failureReasonBreakdown and signInsByStore are returned {OBSERVED}
[BODY] the timeline is returned with a granularity that follows the requested period {OBSERVED}
[BODY] a quiet stretch appears as zero-valued buckets rather than missing points {SPEC}

[DOM] the "Sign-in log" entry is present in the Security section {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the panel titled "ATTEMPTS OVER TIME" is present, together with tiles labelled "SIGN-INS", "FAILED ATTEMPTS", "USERS SIGNED IN", "ON BEHALF" {OBSERVED}
[DOM] panels "TOP IPS BY FAILED ATTEMPTS", "TOP ACCOUNTS BY FAILED ATTEMPTS", "FAILURE REASONS", "SIGN-INS BY STORE" are present {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a numeric count plus a previous-period delta is present on each of the four tiles {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the badge on the "Sign-in log" list blade equals the count shown against that account in "TOP ACCOUNTS BY FAILED ATTEMPTS" {SPEC}
[DOM] every row belongs to that account — accounts that merely contain the same substring are absent {SPEC}
[DOM] the "Search keyword..." box is empty, because the drill-down applies a user filter and not a text search {SPEC}

[DOM] the badge on the "Sign-in log" list blade equals the number on the "ON BEHALF" tile {SPEC}
[DOM] every row shows Type "Impersonation" with outcome "Success" — no "ImpersonationRevert" row, no failed row {SPEC}
[DOM] the filter panel shows Outcome "Success" together with Type "On behalf" {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the row renders the operator, then the "On behalf of" marker, then the customer {SPEC}
[DOM] an ordinary sign-in row shows the user alone, with no "On behalf of" marker {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the "Outcome" column and the "Type" column are populated on every row {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the card shows "Success" and "On behalf" as badges {OBSERVED}
[DOM] fields "Date", "User", "Operator", "Operator ID", "User ID", "Member ID", "IP address", "Host", "User agent", "Store" are present {OBSERVED}
[DOM] no editable input is present on the card — every value renders as read-only text {SPEC}
[DOM] no separate "Outcome" field duplicates the badge {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the widget shows a count of that account's attempts {OBSERVED}
[DOM] opening it shows only that account's activity {SPEC}
[DOM] the "Active sessions" widget is present beside it, listing the sessions that are live now {OBSERVED}

[DOM] the Type list offers "All", "Password", "External provider", "On behalf", "On behalf revert", "Sign out" {SPEC}
[DOM] choosing "On behalf" returns grants only; choosing "On behalf revert" returns reverts only {SPEC}
[DOM] the period selector offers "30 min", "1 hour", "6 hours", "24 hours", "7 days", "30 days", "All time", "Custom" {OBSERVED}

[DOM] a banner is present stating that new attempts are not being recorded, naming "Settings › Platform › Sign In Log" {SPEC}
[DOM] the banner also states that "Login on behalf is always recorded" {SPEC}
[DOM] records written before the switch was turned off are still present in the list {OBSERVED}

[BODY] the over-length user agent is stored truncated rather than failing the write {SPEC}
[BODY] the over-length user name is stored truncated {SPEC}
[BODY] the ordinary attempt in the same batch is recorded too — one bad value does not discard its neighbours {SPEC}

[BODY] the account is gone from the user search {OBSERVED}
[BODY] its audit records are still returned, with the same count as before the deletion {SPEC}
[BODY] the records keep the userId of the deleted account, so the history stays attributable {SPEC}
